From a9a0aa27f04cd6246b1bff7753c49c0d88981fde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Srinidhi Rao <srinidhi.rao@broadcom.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:32:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] lighttpd: honor openssl system default TLS groups

  -  When no Groups/Curves is set via ssl.openssl.ssl-conf-cmd, mod_openssl
unconditionally calls SSL_CTX_set1_groups_list() with a compiled-in
default ("X25519:P-256:P-384:X448"; upstream 1.4.83+ prepends
"X25519MLKEM768:"). This overrides the openssl.cnf system_default
"Groups" policy, and the unprefixed X25519/X448 entries are a hard error
when they are not available.

    The openssl 3.5.x FIPS provider registers X25519/X448 with fips=no, so
with default_properties = fips=yes SSL_CTX_set1_groups_list() fails,
lighttpd logs "SSL: Unable to config groups X25519:P-256:P-384:X448" and
TLS socket initialization aborts. The failure happens before
ssl.openssl.ssl-conf-cmd is processed, so it cannot be worked around
from lighttpd.conf.

    With openssl >= 3.5, skip the override when no groups are configured, as
is already done for BoringSSL/LibreSSL. SSL_CTX_new() has already applied
the system_default policy, and openssl's own built-in default
("?*X25519MLKEM768 / ?*X25519:?secp256r1 / ...") marks every group '?'.
An explicit ssl.openssl.ssl-conf-cmd "Groups"/"Curves" is still applied.

[Srinidhi: Photon-specific fix, not present in upstream.]

Signed-off-by: Srinidhi Rao <srinidhi.rao@broadcom.com>
---
 src/mod_openssl.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mod_openssl.c b/src/mod_openssl.c
index 26517ae1..620d7161 100644
--- a/src/mod_openssl.c
+++ b/src/mod_openssl.c
@@ -3339,6 +3339,20 @@ mod_openssl_ssl_conf_curves(server *srv, plugin_config_socket *s, const buffer *
         return 1;
   #endif
 
+  #if !defined(BORINGSSL_API_VERSION) && !defined(LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER) \
+   && OPENSSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x30500000L
+    /* openssl 3.5+ applies the openssl.cnf system_default "Groups" policy in
+     * SSL_CTX_new(), and its built-in default group list marks every group
+     * with '?' (ignore if unavailable).  Do not override either with a
+     * hardcoded list containing unprefixed X25519/X448: the openssl 3.5 FIPS
+     * provider registers X25519/X448 as fips=no, so with
+     * default_properties = fips=yes SSL_CTX_set1_groups_list() fails and the
+     * TLS socket cannot be initialized.  Groups can still be set explicitly
+     * with ssl.openssl.ssl-conf-cmd = ("Groups" => "...") */
+    if (NULL == ssl_ec_curve || buffer_is_blank(ssl_ec_curve))
+        return 1;
+  #endif
+
   #if (defined(BORINGSSL_API_VERSION) && BORINGSSL_API_VERSION >= 3) \
    || (defined(LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER) \
        && LIBRESSL_VERSION_NUMBER >= 0x2050100fL) \
-- 
2.53.0

